 "note": "A partner (Claude, 2026-11-18): a crescent that cups a Cunabella's arm. Its body holds the nucleus; two curved horns (lobes, each with a tip turned inward) hold a nitroplast and a plastid, oil in both tips; a Partner pad on the inside of the curve; no chamber, no tail; rests in the dark. Joined, it feeds its host nitrogen (Trade about 0.04-0.13: it gives far more than it gets) and is carried toward the light; its host divides about 2 days sooner and sheds it around day 2, once its own oil runs low. Alone it sinks and starved on all three seeds tried (day 3-4); after a stay on a host all three were alive at day 4. Put it in the tank beside a Cunabella: free Partner pads pull each other within 15 µm."
